window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>They lost their forever. She never believed in it. Fate had other ideas.</b></p> <p><b>Genesis</b></p> <p>Genesis Valentine knows exactly what she wants out of life. As a decorated journalist, she is determined to tell stories that matter and to make a difference in the world. Unfortunately, as an unbonded omega, she's considered a liability in the field. If she wants to take her career to the next level, she has to show her editor that she can get her scent under control. And that means taking on a pack, at least temporarily.</p> <p>At almost thirty, Genesis should've been bonded years ago, but she refuses to be a slave to societal expectations or even biological needs. She has no interest in being owned by a bunch of alphaholes who would try to control her life and interfere with her plans. So, when she's matched with a temporary pack of widowed alphas who have no intention of mating again, Genesis knows she's found the perfect solution to all her problems. However, when she meets the handsome pack of silver foxes, Genesis quickly realizes she might've gotten more than she bargained for.</p> <p><b>Orlando</b></p> <p>Orlando Rossi has built a perfect life. His business is wildly successful, and his packmates' artistic and farming ventures are equally impressive. They have a beautiful home and more money than they can spend. Perfect.</p> <p>Except for the gaping hole where their omega used to be. In the decade since her death, Orlando has done everything he can to get Pack Rossi back on their feet. They've come so far, but he knows something is still missing.</p> <p>When they take on a smart, feisty temporary omega who smells like heaven, Orlando knows immediately that everything is about to change. Unfortunately, both Genesis and Orlando's packmates are stubborn, strong-willed, and set in their ways. Is it too late to find love again, or will Genesis be the fresh start they didn't know they needed?</p> <p><i>Contains mature content. A complete list of content warnings can be found on the author's website.</i></p>"; 
